Orthonym — Third-Party Components
=================================

Orthonym's own source is released under the MIT License.

Orthonym uses two third-party Java programs. They are NOT part of this
repository and are NOT included in any Orthonym package. They are downloaded
from their official releases, on `pip install` or by `orthonym --fetch-jars`,
into the user's cache, and each download is checked against the SHA-256
below before it is used. Each jar keeps its own licence terms, listed here.

Orthonym runs them unmodified, as separate programs on the Java virtual
machine (by default in one in-process JVM via JPype, or as a `java -jar`
subprocess). If either jar is missing, Orthonym stops with an error rather than
naming with less validation; setting ORTHONYM_ALLOW_REDUCED=1 opts in to naming
without them.


